hexagon: htp: silu and swiglu of small inputs in the int16 path
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-kernels/0003-hexagon-htp-activation-int16-tables.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The int16 path of hvx-act-i16.h computes silu(x) = relu(x) - h(|x|), and the
polynomial pieces of h start at the octave 2^-12. A lane with |x| < 2^-12 gets
h = 0 from the table, thus SILU and SWIGLU give x or 0 in place of x/2. Above
2^-12 the int16 step of h (2^-16) is large against a small result. A sweep of
the v79 simulator from 1e-12 to 1e2 gives a relative error of 1.0 in the rows
1e-12 to 1e-3 and 0.014 in the row 1e-3 to 1e-2, with a largest absolute error
of 1.2e-4. The app graphs reach this path: every SILU and SWIGLU of the text
graphs runs it.

This patch gives each lane with |x| < 2^-4 the value x * (0.5 + x/4), whose
relative error is below |x|^3/24. The other lanes keep the table result. After
the patch, the sweep gives at most 1.3e-7 in every row from 1e-12 to 1e-2, and
the rows above do not change. The extra work for each vector is one and, one
compare, two multiplies, one add, two conversions and one mux.

The patch also adds test_silu_small to test-backend-ops: SILU and SWIGLU on
rows from 6.25e-2 down to 6.25e-9, with the largest relative error of one
element as the error.

